            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Oggi."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Told where this Mac is — the Permissions tab asks macOS, and keeps the name of the town and of the region rather than any coordinates — it also knows which regional feed is the local one, and needs no city named to answer about the weather. It cannot name an address of its own — only one of those words — so nothing it reads can send it somewhere else. What comes back is quoted to it as somebody else's words, and an answer built on them is not allowed to open, copy or move anything: a headline is written by a stranger. The request carries no question, no account and no cookies; the site sees that a public feed was fetched. With Apple Intelligence or a model on this Mac the headlines stay here; with ChatGPT, Claude or a Shortcut they are sent on like any other question." : {
      "comment" : "Told where this Mac is — the Permissions tab asks macOS, and keeps the name of the town and of the region rather than any coordinates — it also knows which regional feed is the local one, and needs no city named to answer about the weather. It cannot name an address of its own — only one of those words — so nothing it reads can send it somewhere else. What comes back is quoted to it as somebody else's words, and an answer built on them is not allowed to open, copy or move anything: a headline is written by a stranger. The request carries no question, no account and no cookies; the site sees that a public feed was fetched. With Apple Intelligence or a model on this Mac the headlines stay here; with ChatGPT, Claude or a Shortcut they are sent on like any other question.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Told where this Mac is — the Permissions tab asks macOS, and keeps the name of the town and of the region rather than any coordinates — it also knows which regional feed is the local one, and needs no city named to answer about the weather. It cannot name an address of its own — only one of those words — so nothing it reads can send it somewhere else. What comes back is quoted to it as somebody else's words, and an answer built on them is not allowed to open, copy or move anything: a headline is written by a stranger. The request carries no question, no account and no cookies; the site sees that a public feed was fetched. With Apple Intelligence or a model on this Mac the headlines stay here; with ChatGPT, Claude or a Shortcut they are sent on like any other question."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Si sabe dónde está este Mac —la pestaña Permisos se lo pregunta a macOS y guarda el nombre del municipio y de la región en vez de coordenadas—, también sabe qué fuente regional es la local, y no necesita que le nombres una ciudad para responder sobre el tiempo. No puede indicar una dirección propia —solo una de esas palabras—, así que nada de lo que lee puede mandarlo a otro sitio. Lo que vuelve se le cita como palabras de otros, y una respuesta construida sobre ellas no puede abrir, copiar ni mover nada: un titular lo escribe un desconocido. La petición no lleva la pregunta, ni cuenta ni cookies; el sitio ve que se descargó un feed público. Con Apple Intelligence o un modelo en este Mac los titulares se quedan aquí; con ChatGPT, Claude o un atajo se envían como cualquier otra pregunta."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "S’il sait où se trouve ce Mac — l’onglet Autorisations le demande à macOS, et garde le nom de la commune et de la région plutôt que des coordonnées — il sait aussi quel flux régional est le flux local, et n’a pas besoin qu’on lui nomme une ville pour répondre sur la météo. Il ne peut pas indiquer une adresse à lui — seulement l’un de ces mots — donc rien de ce qu’il lit ne peut l’envoyer ailleurs. Ce qui revient lui est cité comme les mots de quelqu’un d’autre, et une réponse fondée là-dessus n’a pas le droit d’ouvrir, de copier ni de déplacer quoi que ce soit : un titre est écrit par un inconnu. La requête ne transporte ni question, ni compte, ni cookies ; le site voit qu’un flux public a été récupéré. Avec Apple Intelligence ou un modèle sur ce Mac, les titres restent ici ; avec ChatGPT, Claude ou un raccourci, ils sont envoyés comme n’importe quelle question."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Se sa dove si trova questo Mac — la scheda Autorizzazioni lo chiede a macOS, e tiene il nome del comune e della regione invece di qualsiasi coordinata — sa anche quale feed regionale è quello locale, e non ha bisogno che gli dici la città per risponderti sul tempo. Non può indicare un indirizzo suo — solo una di quelle parole — quindi niente di quello che legge può mandarlo altrove. Quello che torna gli viene citato come parole di altri, e una risposta costruita su quelle non può aprire, copiare o spostare niente: un titolo lo scrive uno sconosciuto. La richiesta non porta la domanda, né account né cookie; il sito vede che è stato scaricato un feed pubblico. Con Apple Intelligence o un modello su questo Mac i titoli restano qui; con ChatGPT, Claude o un comando rapido vengono spediti come qualunque altra domanda."
          }
        }
      }
    },
